# Local environment overrides
#
# NOTE: `.env` itself is intentionally NOT ignored. DI-1 commits it with a development
# default so a clean clone runs with `docker compose up` and no manual step, which makes
# the Neo4j password public by construction. That is a deliberate, local-only decision —
# see docs/specs/SPEC-001-di-1-policy-grapher.md (Environment Variables).
# Adding `.env` here would break first-run setup; it must change before any shared
# deployment, and that change belongs in an ADR, not in this file.
.env.local
.env.*.local
